    "mcp_tool_description": "Set how servers on one network get their IP address, then verify it with determine_ip_provider, the call the order form and provisioning use. onb_addressing: dhcp, static, or both (the requester picks DHCP or a typed IP per order). static and both need onb_gateway and onb_netmask (255.255.255.0 or 24); onb_dns1, onb_dns2 and onb_dns_domain are optional. For static, onb_ip_source says where addresses come from: pool (a CloudBolt IP pool on the network, from onb_pool_range such as 10.0.5.10-10.0.5.60 or a list; checked for free addresses), ipam (onb_ipam names an IPAM endpoint the user added in the UI at /setup/add-ipam/; the tool checks its connection, enables its orchestration action, and when the network is not yet mapped returns needsUiStep with the IPAM Networks tab link), or manual (the requester types sc_nic_0_ip on each order). Only one source stays on the network: choosing dhcp, both, manual or ipam removes an unused IP pool, and anything but ipam clears an IPAM link. With only onb_network it returns the current settings and the IPAM endpoints. Runs as a job: poll the returned id with fetch_job. Requires a CloudBolt admin caller.",
    "mcp_tool_name": "onb_network_addressing",
    "mcp_tool_title": ""
